  "homepage": "https://github.com/EsDmitrii/kconmon-ng",
  "description": "kubectl-kconmon talks to a running kconmon-ng controller's HTTP API through\na client-go port-forward, so operators can inspect the cluster's node/zone\ntopology and run one-shot connectivity diagnostics between any two nodes\nwithout opening Grafana: TCP, UDP, ICMP, DNS, HTTP, a path MTU probe\n(--type pmtu) and MTR per-hop traces. It requires kconmon-ng to be\ninstalled in the cluster.\n\nExamples:\n  kubectl kconmon topology\n  kubectl kconmon check node-1 node-2 --type icmp\n  kubectl kconmon check node-1 node-2 --type pmtu\n  kubectl kconmon mtr node-1 node-2\n\nDocs: https://esdmitrii.github.io/kconmon-ng/\n",
